Description: avcodec/decode: clear queried hardware state when choosing software
 A get_format callback can successfully query hardware frame parameters
 and then select a software format. The query leaves hwaccel_priv_data
 allocated, although no hwaccel is initialized. Frame-threaded HEVC
 decoding then aborts when updating a worker context.
 .
 Uninitialize the unused hardware state when a software format is
 selected, as is already done on error.
 .
 Assisted-by: gpt-6.1-sol via Codex
 Assisted-by: gpt-6-astra via Codex
 .
 Carried from pull request 25398 (still open). The edition shipped the same one-line change since +stereo3d6 as its own patch; this replaces that patch with the pull request's commit, whose test is patch 0067.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, https://code.ffmpeg.org/danielcamposramos/FFmpeg/commit/60f372459e2631964e3d8d2c17e7bf95fac195c3
Forwarded: https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/25398
Last-Update: 2026-11-05

diff --git a/libavcodec/decode.c b/libavcodec/decode.c
index 3f1dfac..0cd8477 100644
--- a/libavcodec/decode.c
+++ b/libavcodec/decode.c
@@ -1357,7 +1357,9 @@ int ff_get_format(AVCodecContext *avctx, const enum AVPixelFormat *fmt)
         --n;
     }
 
-    if (ret < 0)
+    // A successful hardware frame query can leave private state behind
+    // even when the callback chooses a software format.
+    if (ret < 0 || !(desc->flags & AV_PIX_FMT_FLAG_HWACCEL))
         ff_hwaccel_uninit(avctx);
 
     av_freep(&choices);
